#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26bf521e-2e91-5208-9ac2-211ba3f34c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos(5t)+\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383343} {:answer/id #uuid "ef003f15-1358-5eb9-84f5-758637d1473c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cos(5t)+\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef003f15-1358-5eb9-84f5-758637d1473c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cos(5t)+\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383344} :answer-field/id #uuid "49a6e944-8bd8-5c24-bd49-e7c952c9fd6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8f1c554-6115-5329-b181-329f633fe465" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin(5t)+\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8f1c554-6115-5329-b181-329f633fe465" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin(5t)+\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383346} :answer-field/id #uuid "e44a5aaa-4023-5526-9086-ebe65b15de5b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29054d88-29fd-5238-a340-8f5e32c893bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-335260" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\, \\\\ \\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e760635-3e99-5199-94da-ca122920eed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383349} {:answer/id #uuid "1c11745f-8eb5-5026-8f56-6684ba4f1b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383350} {:answer/id #uuid "83fbfd05-8982-5353-8708-9cfe8e9c32ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383351} {:answer/id #uuid "6c968feb-b575-5f82-9743-0acbbb35a1d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -7\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383352} {:answer/id #uuid "474eff3c-6a82-5cf4-85a8-5e69bafa1119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e760635-3e99-5199-94da-ca122920eed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383349} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f0c10ec-56dc-5b75-8ddf-715ba10fc5e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a832f4b-3d78-50eb-96fa-49288eaea4c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-335265" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c863fe-870d-5313-9392-c320183e66ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin(8t+8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383356} {:answer/id #uuid "700ff51d-7a70-583e-8a1c-4a17c04206bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin(8t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08c863fe-870d-5313-9392-c320183e66ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin(8t+8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383356} :answer-field/id #uuid "96b6d1d5-6f90-5bc1-b84d-f468e1c345ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383355} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55cf4ee5-9920-5791-abd8-fb750fbfb11e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos(8t+8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55cf4ee5-9920-5791-abd8-fb750fbfb11e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos(8t+8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383359} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6edef63-0ad7-5ad1-8687-3176ef8dcf4a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e85d2c3-146c-56f3-8bc8-f5056ea2c36c" :question/math-academy-id "q-335437" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=8y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-8x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-1) \\\\ y(-1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+1)}\\,x(-1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1))\\, \\\\ \\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3bf7fd4-0ade-513a-86b6-dc0bb7dedbbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383362} {:answer/id #uuid "7500048a-aa55-5b56-9fa2-8d92dae7d8d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383363} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a8192b-8b09-55c4-b19c-7fba816ab0fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383364} {:answer/id #uuid "c1483b33-6150-5020-803a-0971248aaae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383365} {:answer/id #uuid "56c8bc58-857b-51be-92ed-ea74101846f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7a8192b-8b09-55c4-b19c-7fba816ab0fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383364} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b966142-a05a-5f61-b7ea-0dca1ce7709e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17140ce0-7f0a-5578-9bb0-2e4e6a2676d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-335449" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8d2d12-bf9d-5eca-b206-dbc5b4a6cdfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383369} {:answer/id #uuid "382ce1b5-4701-5ccf-bf5e-54da6094ea3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a solution curve" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383370} {:answer/id #uuid "e8559e23-609a-5003-be7e-a5815309fc08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of the determinant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383371} {:answer/id #uuid "7d5fc4b8-810f-502c-bfbf-f81746b1d55a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c8d2d12-bf9d-5eca-b206-dbc5b4a6cdfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383369} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aba4aa6-1e78-5bc7-b87d-4917c8f15ee4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383368} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "542638ec-fb88-5201-b4ec-c80c79e15318" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying the chain rule to ${Φ}_{0}(0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383374} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd2c33-e383-5364-96d1-b34e769eb292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ at $t=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383375} {:answer/id #uuid "81a5315b-a232-5574-b779-87ae77a901d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "computing $det({Φ}_{0}(0))$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383376} {:answer/id #uuid "d936344c-0e61-59f6-9494-196ee3bb3d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using the initial condition ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d936344c-0e61-59f6-9494-196ee3bb3d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using the initial condition ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383377} :answer-field/id #uuid "00e1f780-27de-5c5e-8e15-fe9443bb506b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eede47d-1f4a-5116-bfe4-78654a9a0181" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383379} {:answer/id #uuid "eb272981-013f-508e-bc1e-e022b043ccb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383380} {:answer/id #uuid "73df5fe9-6b8f-5b2d-bc3c-12066e211aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383381} {:answer/id #uuid "b716d6a7-52cf-5a97-8cb8-4856ffe801e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb272981-013f-508e-bc1e-e022b043ccb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383380} :answer-field/id #uuid "8649a74b-e664-51e6-8921-a77407d97b34" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1ccc151-bceb-5b28-9e4f-95f3bdc90690" :question/math-academy-id "q-336481" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ By definition, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ satisfies the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nThe second condition here is exactly line $\\text{L4},$ so $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by $\\text{using the initial condition }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$"}]}
